      "heading": "Regulatory basis",
      "body": "",
      "tables": [
        {
          "caption": "",
          "columns": [
            "Reference",
            "Requirement",
            "How the plan meets it"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "DORA Art. 6(4)",
              "Assign the management and oversight of ICT risk to a control function with an appropriate level of independence, segregated from the first line and from internal audit.",
              "The 2LoD CISO Office plans, tests and concludes; asset owners (1LoD) attest their own data; Internal Audit (3LoD) is informed and not part of the testing."
            ],
            [
              "DORA Art. 8(1)",
              "Identify, classify and document the ICT assets that support the business functions, and review the classification at least yearly.",
              "Every Tier 1 and Tier 2 asset's Security NFR data is attested by its owner and data-quality reviewed by 2LoD within the year, in quarterly waves."
            ],
            [
              "DORA Art. 8(4); RTS (EU) 2024/1774 Arts. 4–5",
              "Identify all ICT assets, map those considered critical and their interdependencies, under an ICT asset management policy and procedure.",
              "The scope population is extracted from the ICT asset inventory, reconciled to the critical or important function mapping, and frozen before the first draw."
            ],
            [
              "DORA Art. 24(6)",
              "Test the ICT systems and applications that support critical or important functions at least yearly.",
              "Tier 1 assets support a critical or important function and are sample-tested against the Security NFRs every quarter. This complements the resilience testing programme; it does not replace it."
            ],
            [
              "DORA Art. 6(5); RTS (EU) 2024/1774 Art. 27",
              "Review the ICT risk management framework at least yearly, and report on the review to the competent authority on request.",
              "The annual conclusion goes to the ICT Risk Committee and the management body as an input to the framework review report."
            ]
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "limitations": "This report is prepared by the 2LoD CISO Office (ICT risk control function) for the ICT Risk Committee, from the records of assurance plan AP-2027-001 as they stood on 14 Jan 2028. It does not reflect changes made after that date. Coverage is measured from the attestation and data-quality review dates recorded in the plan. Testing is on samples, which gives reasonable rather than absolute assurance. Results not signed off by QA are provisional. Findings are reported as Audit Findings holds them on the report date; their remediation is followed up there. The conclusion is the control function's on the tests performed. It is not an opinion on the design or operation of controls outside the plan's scope, and it does not replace the work of the other assurance plans, such as resilience testing, or of internal audit."
